            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Russian for to embroider, then the Russian for lace."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: нитка",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "нитка (nítka) — \"a thread\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Нужна чёрная нитка, чтобы пришить пуговицу. Nuzhná chyórnaya nítka, chtóby prishít púgovitsu. I need black thread to sew the button on."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine; genitive plural ниток. A diminutive of нить."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "нитка (nítka) is a diminutive of нить 'thread'; EtymDB lists нитка (nítka) without a source, and нить is inherited from Proto-Slavic nitь (EtymDB)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
