              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "напёрсток (napyórstok) — \"a thimble\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Без напёрстка я всегда колю палец. Bez napyórstka ya vsegdá kolyú pálets. Without a thimble I always prick my finger."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Masculine; genitive напёрстка."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "напёрсток (napyórstok) is inherited from Proto-Slavic napьrstъkъ, derived from pьrstъ 'finger' (EtymDB): a cap on the finger. The old word перст 'finger', which EtymDB marks as a Church Slavonic borrowing, is usually linked to перчатки 'gloves'."
            }
          ]
        },
